      "id": "b_essay_open",
      "type": "prose",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "id": "quote_essay_tldr",
          "kind": "quote",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "paragraph",
              "content": [
                { "type": "text", "marks": [{ "type": "bold" }], "text": "TL;DR" },
                { "type": "text", "text": ": After walking away from the banking idea, I went looking for what to build, and mostly learned how easily I over-abstract. The fix that stuck: stop chasing pain, which is invisible and stretches to fit anything, and start chasing the workarounds people have already built." }
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "id": "h2_essay_looking",
          "kind": "h2",
          "content": [{ "type": "text", "text": "After I walked away, I had to actually go looking" }]
        },
        {
          "id": "p_essay_looking",
          "kind": "p",
          "content": [
            { "type": "text", "text": "Last time I wrote about catching myself chasing an impressive-sounding idea I didn't actually want, and what that revealed about how I choose things. Walking away was the easy part to write about. The harder part is what comes after: a blank page, and the genuinely uncomfortable job of finding something " },
            { "type": "text", "marks": [{ "type": "italic" }], "text": "real" },
            { "type": "text", "text": " to point at." }
          ]
        },
        {
          "id": "p_essay_anchor",
          "kind": "p",
          "content": [
            { "type": "text", "text": "Most of what I've learned so far isn't about the world yet. It's about my own thinking, which is a less flattering subject and a more useful one. The " },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "marks": [
                {
                  "type": "link",
                  "attrs": {
                    "href": "https://jinhyuk.org/essays/whos-choosing/",
                    "target": "_blank",
                    "rel": "noopener noreferrer"
                  }
                }
              ],
              "text": "previous essay"
            },
            { "type": "text", "text": " is where the thread starts." }
          ]
        },
        {
          "id": "h3_essay_rule",
          "kind": "h3",
          "content": [{ "type": "text", "text": "The rule I ended up with" }]
        },
        {
          "id": "ul_essay_rule",
          "kind": "ul",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "listItem",
              "content": [
                {
                  "type": "paragraph",
                  "content": [
                    { "type": "text", "text": "A workaround is proof the pain is " },
                    { "type": "text", "marks": [{ "type": "textStyle", "attrs": { "color": "#ff5722" } }], "text": "real" },
                    { "type": "text", "text": "." }
                  ]
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "listItem",
              "content": [
                {
                  "type": "paragraph",
                  "content": [{ "type": "text", "text": "It proves the pain recurs, because nobody builds a workaround for a one-off." }]
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "listItem",
              "content": [
                {
                  "type": "paragraph",
                  "content": [{ "type": "text", "text": "And it proves the pain already costs something, because the workaround itself costs something." }]
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
